meta {
  name: Create Watchlist
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/watchlist?name=stocks
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

params:query {
  name: stocks
}

body:json {
  {
    "duration": 12000,
    "staleAfter": 2700,
    "staleBehavior": "dim",
    "rows": [
      { "symbol": "SpaceX", "icon": "spacex", "value": 184.2, "currency": "USD", "change": 3.42 },
      { "symbol": "Meta", "icon": "meta", "value": 612.85, "currency": "USD", "change": -1.08 },
      { "symbol": "Nvidia", "icon": "nvidia", "value": 143.07, "currency": "USD", "change": 0.56 },
      { "symbol": "PEA Monde", "icon": "etf", "value": 28.41, "currency": "EUR", "change": -0.32 },
      { "symbol": "Apple", "icon": "apple", "value": 231.6, "currency": "USD", "change": 1.21 },
      { "symbol": "Bitcoin", "icon": "bitcoin", "value": 98452.3, "currency": "USD", "change": 2.14 }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Creates or updates a watchlist app: a list of quotes, one 21-pixel row each,
  three rows per page, with a vertical dot carousel on the right edge when there
  are more.

  The watchlist name in the query param becomes the unique key, max 13 chars: a
  longer name is refused with HTTP 400 ("Watchlist name too long (max 13)")
  rather than shortened, since the shortened key and the app ID would stop
  matching. App ID in rotation is prefixed with "watchlist_" (e.g.
  "watchlist_stocks"). Two watchlists can exist at a time (MAX_WATCHLIST_APPS).

  Parameters:
  - rows: Up to 9 rows, three per page. More than 9 is refused with HTTP 400
    and the watchlist keeps the rows it had. Without rows, the stored rows stay. A page
    holding fewer than three rows shares the screen height between them
  - duration: Display duration in ms (default: 10000), split evenly across the
    carousel pages
  - staleAfter: Silence tolerated before the watchlist is stale, in seconds
    (default: 3600)
  - staleBehavior: "hide", "dim" (default), "badge" or "none". With dim and
    badge, STALE replaces the change of the first row of every page

  Row fields:
  - symbol: Name on the top line, max 15 chars. A name wider than the room the
    change leaves scrolls inside it. Latin-1 accents are shown as their closest
    ASCII letter
  - symbolColor: Color of the symbol (default: "#FFB000")
  - icon: Icon name from /icons folder (optional), drawn 8x8 one pixel from the
    left edge
  - value: Price, formatted like the tracker value on six characters beside a
    three-letter currency
  - currency: Label in grey right after the price, max 7 chars (e.g. "USD")
  - change: Percentage, two decimals with its sign, green from zero up, red below
}
